#. ~ Description of "adult wildwood weaver"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "This weaver is fully grown.  There's no light behind its eyes, yet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "adult wildwood weaver"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The %s awakens.  It gazes at you with its many eyes, ready to serve you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "awoken wildwood weaver"
msgid_plural "awoken wildwood weavers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "awoken wildwood weaver"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid ""
"You never thought you'd see the day when a wildwood entity would be so "
"playful and docile.  This weaver is ready to serve you, and can be used to "
"repair clothing or create a shelter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "small damaged weaver"
msgid_plural "small damaged weavers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "small damaged weaver"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid ""
"A tiny broken weaver.  Its legs bent and broken, it can no longer be used to "
"repair clothing or create a shelter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "small wildwood stag beetle ball"
msgid_plural "small wildwood stag beetle balls"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "small wildwood stag beetle ball"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid ""
"A small ball made of wildwood.  A narrative relief of a stag beetle dancing "
"wraps the ball.  A soft chittering noise can be heard from it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "small wildwood stag beetle ball"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The %s surges in size.  It shudders and rolls around as the relief begins to "
"move on its own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "small wildwood stag beetle
#. ball"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "The beetle does not have enough liquid to grow."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "small wildwood stag beetle ball"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "The beetle isn't done growing yet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "wildwood stag beetle ball"
msgid_plural "wildwood stag beetle balls"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "wildwood stag beetle ball"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid ""
"A large ball made of wildwood.  A narrative relief of a dancing stag beetle "
"wraps the ball.  A soft chittering noise can be heard from it as the relief "
"flows across the surface."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid "wildwood rune"
msgid_plural "wildwood runes"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "wildwood rune"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/druid_items.json
msgid ""
"A small druid rune wrapped in a leaf.  It appears to be made of some kind of "
"resin, and is very sticky."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Bag of Infinite Throwing Knives"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted.json
msgid ""
"This bag conjures a magical throwing knife on activation.  Only refills when "
"worn.  It also boosts your throwing abilities."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_boots.json
msgid "pair of boots of elvenkind"
msgid_plural "pairs of boots of elvenkind"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "pair of boots of elvenkind"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_boots.json
msgid ""
"One of the traditional items of the ancient elven warrior societies, these "
"soft leather boots are worked with silver inlays in the shape of vines and "
"leaves.  They allow the wearer to walk in complete silence and move faster "
"when in the wilderness."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "disorientation bracelet"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracelet.json
msgid ""
"Known as \"a worse version of petrification bracelet\", this tool casts a "
"spell that temporarily breaks the whole movement system of a creature, "
"disabling its movement for a short time.  Require almost a week to restore "
"its charge."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "propulsion bracelet"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracelet.json
msgid ""
"It feels like the world around you just stops.  That's not true, that's just "
"a combination of really fast speed and some mana tricks you can't understand."
"  Requires a whole week to restore its charge."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracelet.json
msgid "inert mana-leech shackle"
msgid_plural "inert mana-leech shackles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "inert mana-leech shackle"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracelet.json
msgid ""
"A platinum bracelet covered in runes.  If it was active, it would keep its "
"wearer from casting spells.  Now it's just another useless trinket as you do "
"not know the spells it requires to be activated again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracelet.json
msgid "mana-leech shackle"
msgid_plural "mana-leech shackles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "mana-leech shackle"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracelet.json
msgid ""
"A platinum bracelet covered in runes.  It cannot be removed without the "
"appropriate spell and it constantly drains the wearer's mana, preventing them"
" from casting any spell until they get rid of it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracers.json
msgid "pair of bracers of archery"
msgid_plural "pairs of bracers of archery"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "pair of bracers of archery"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracers.json
msgid ""
"A set of leather bracers worked with images of arrows in flight and scenes of"
" hunting parties.  Bows you wield will be more accurate and do more damage "
"while you wear these, and you can shoot your arrows farther as well."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracers.json
msgid "bracers of the blinding strike"
msgid_plural "bracers of the blinding strike"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "bracers of the blinding strike"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_bracers.json
msgid ""
"A pair of light leather bracers with inlays of mithril looking like vines "
"with tiny, leaf-shaped leaves branching off of the vines.  It slightly "
"increases your attack speed at all times, and you may activate it to greatly "
"increase your attack speed for a short time."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Wildshape Cloak: Fish"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_cloaks.json
msgid ""
"A magical cloak that shimmers like fresh water under a warm sun.  It can be "
"worn to morph your body to a form that is excellent for swimming, but ill-"
"suited for combat.  You should probably stand in water before you put it on."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Wildshape Cloak: Deer"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_cloaks.json
msgid ""
"A magical cloak that feels soft to the touch.  It can be worn to morph your "
"body to a form well-suited to escaping difficult situations.  However, it is "
"not suited for combat."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_cloaks.json
msgid "cloak of elvenkind"
msgid_plural "cloaks of elvenkind"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "cloak of elvenkind"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_cloaks.json
msgid ""
"One of the traditional items of the ancient elven warrior societies, this "
"cloth cloak woven with still-living leaves makes its wearer much harder to "
"spot in forests or dense vegetation.  Infamous for their use during the "
"Vietnam War by elves on both sides of the conflict."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "enchanted parabolan wool blouse"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A loose silvery iridescent blouse in a style most often associated with "
"pirates and renfaires.  It shimmers as you look at it.  Made of parabolan "
"wool, it sometimes dimly shows reflections of things here and not.  This "
"particular one has piratical flairs and glitters with enchantment."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "enchanted parabolan wool breeches"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A well-made pair of old-fashioned pants, made of silvery iridescent material."
"  Comfortable, but lacks pockets.  It shimmers as you look at it.  Made of "
"parabolan wool, it sometimes dimly shows reflections of things here and not."
"  This particular one has piratical flairs and glitters with enchantment."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "parabolan wool blouse"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A loose silvery iridescent blouse in a style most often associated with "
"pirates and renfaires.  It shimmers as you look at it.  Made of parabolan "
"wool, it sometimes dimly shows reflections of things here and not."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "parabolan wool breeches"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A well-made pair of old-fashioned pants, made of silvery iridescent material."
"  Comfortable, but lacks pockets.  It shimmers as you look at it.  Made of "
"parabolan wool, it sometimes dimly shows reflections of things here and not."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid "parabolan wool gambeson"
msgid_plural "parabolan wool gambesons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "parabolan wool gambeson"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A padded greatcoat assembled by quilting rarely available iridescent wool "
"that was intended as standalone armor, this is half the thickness of a "
"historical gambeson due to the quality of its material.  Famed for its "
"resistance to arrows in olden times, one might wonder how effective it might "
"be against modern projectiles."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid "thin-sleeved parabolan wool gambeson"
msgid_plural "thin-sleeved parabolan wool gambesons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "thin-sleeved parabolan wool gambeson"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A thick iridescent wool greatcoat famed for its resistance to arrows in olden"
" times.  Compared to conventional wool, this is much lighter and less warm.  "
"The sleeves are a lot thinner for flexibility and it drapes below your legs, "
"providing additional protection there."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid "sleeveless parabolan wool gambeson"
msgid_plural "sleeveless parabolan wool gambesons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "sleeveless parabolan wool gambeson"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A thick iridescent wool surcoat famed for its resistance to arrows in the "
"olden times.  Compared to conventional wool, this is much lighter and less "
"warm.  It drapes below your legs, providing additional protection there, and "
"it lacks sleeves entirely."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid "parabolan wool heavy arming pants"
msgid_plural "pairs of parabolan wool heavy arming pants"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "parabolan wool heavy arming pants"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"Tough, fairly thick iridescent wool pants worn on their own alongside a "
"gambeson.  These are made of layered wool quilting offering very solid "
"protection, specifically for the purposes of stopping arrows."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid "parabolan wool arming mittens"
msgid_plural "pairs of parabolan wool arming mittens"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "parabolan wool arming mittens"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"Thick iridescent wool gauntlets worn in lieu of metal or leather armor.  "
"These are much less encumbering and warm than conventional wool, but they "
"offer excellent protection against arrows."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid "enchanted lab coat"
msgid_plural "enchanted lab coat"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "enchanted lab coat"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A long white coat with several large pockets, with a pentagram on the lapel "
"and a few orichalcum threads sewn into the seams.  Perfect for the stylish-"
"but-effective academic mage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid "enspelled lab coat"
msgid_plural "enspelled lab coat"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of "enspelled lab coat"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_clothes.json
msgid ""
"A long white coat with several large pockets, with a pentagram on the lapel "
"and orichalcum and mithril threads sewn into the seams.  A director of "
"thaumaturgical research would have worn this or something like this before "
"the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "mana laser sight (rail)"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "mana laser sight (underbarrel)"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_gunmods.json
msgid "You rotate the laser sight."
msgstr ""

